25,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems that broad, descriptive projects have a longer life than those chasing specific mechanisms. I also noticed that live breeding colonies often cause delays.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings suggest a shortage of phenotyping technicians, though the glasshouse staff is stable. Interestingly, modelling expertise is available in numbers, but the senior analysts are currently away.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"I've found that the animal facilities are in good shape, but the glasshouses are completely full. Also, the spectroscopy suite has suffered significant downtime due to staffing.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears the agency is generous with computing and glasshouse subsidies, but animal-unit costs have spiked. Shipping is also becoming a burden on the awardee.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I'm concerned about field sites; many were hit by disasters recently. Combined with the breeding colony delays Shizue mentioned, it seems outdoor or live-animal work is quite risky.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, that is a very helpful observation. It makes me lean toward projects that are more stable in their environment.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"If the glasshouse crew is strong but the facilities are fully booked, as Victoria noted, any project requiring greenhouse space might face a bottleneck.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Victoria,,Exactly. The lack of spectroscopy maintenance is also a red flag for any project relying heavily on that specific instrumentation.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,Logic suggests we should favor projects that utilize the currently subsidized computing resources and avoid the rising costs of animal housing.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Midori,,I agree. We should look for a balance where the science can actually proceed without these external interruptions.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
