50,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Candidate D is a catalogue-style project. Based on the closeout files, these tend to provide lasting value and avoid the pitfalls of mechanism-focused studies.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Candidate A requires glasshouses, which are fully booked. Candidate B needs animal facilities, but we lack phenotyping technicians. Candidate C needs spectroscopy, which is unreliable.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Victoria,,I agree with Ryuji. Candidate C is too risky given the instrumentation logs. Candidate A is impossible if the glasshouses are booked solid.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate D avoids the animal-unit cost spikes and the glasshouse bottleneck. It also aligns with the current efficiency of the national repository.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Candidate D involves field samples, but the repository is now fast. However, the field sites are unstable. Still, it seems safer than the others.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, the atlas approach is more resilient than a specific mechanism study. I believe D is our most reliable choice.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"I concur. D relies on sequencing and metadata, which fits the current staffing trends in modelling and code better than phenotyping.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Victoria,,The lack of available glasshouse space effectively eliminates A. The spectroscopy issues eliminate C. D is the most rational choice.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. D utilizes the strengths of the current system while avoiding the financial and logistical traps of the other three.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Midori,,"I feel more comfortable with D now. It provides a broad resource for the community, which is a lovely way to ensure the grant's success.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
